# Graph engineering task loop (local usage)

Use this graph pattern when the user asks for planning/execution across multiple steps, reviewers, or explicit quality gates.

## Activation

Activate graph loop when either is true:
- user explicitly asks for planning with multiple deliverables/roles, or
- user marks bug/RCA mode explicitly (`bug:`, `[bug]`, `rca:`).

Do not activate for trivial one-shot tasks.

## Graph

```
Task -> Planner -> Worker -> Reviewer 1..N -> Synthesize -> Pass?
  -> no: feedback -> Worker (bounded loop)
  -> yes: actionable output -> Plan Reviewer -> User
```

## Output contract per node

- Planner: scoped plan + acceptance criteria + risks.
- Worker: artifact/evidence only for assigned subtask.
- Reviewers: structured verdict (`PASS|PARTIAL|FAIL|BLOCKED`) and exact issues.
- Synthesize: merged verdict and prioritized fix list.
- Plan Reviewer: final packaging quality check.

## Hard constraints

- Keep reviewer independent from worker (no self-verification).
- Use structured router outputs; avoid free-text branching.
- Cap loops (`max_revisions`, recursion limit) to avoid cost blowups.
- Gate side effects (commit/push/deploy) behind explicit user approval.
- Track request count and stop/escalate at configured budget limits.

## Required user input template

```text
Task: <one line goal>
Mode: planning | execution | bug
Scope: <repos/files/services>
Acceptance criteria: <bullet list>
Constraints: <token/time/risk>
Resources: <paths/ids/log lines>
Allowed side effects: <none|commit|push|deploy>
```
